# DDR follow-up RED transcript — batch 2026-10-10-perf-batch (unit PERFDDR2)

DDR conditions applied after the architect (Claude Opus) + qa-reviewer (Claude Sonnet)
approve-with-conditions pass. Two test-only changes were landed first:

1. qa MED-2 — `tests/test_perf_layout_memo.py` `[title]` arm gains a RENDERER-LEVEL
   full-text compare (`screen.renderer.render(screen.graph, state).plain` vs a fresh
   `LayeredRenderer` at the app's own `_view_state`), because the region-clipped canvas
   compare is blind to geometry that never reaches the viewport (measured at 118x34:
   the fold-tree canvas is header-only, `r2-red.transcript` §5).
2. qa LOW-4 — `tests/test_perf_paint_clip.py` `WIRE_CAP` tightened 1,200,000 -> 61,500
   = 5x the measured 12,264 (61,320), rounded up; derivation stated in the node's
   docstring.

All runs: `python -B -m pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider <node>` from the worktree root.
Product mutations are transient; every restore is checked by sha256 (§0, §7).

