## 2 · RED proof M-R2c — cache the SCALED layout (qa MED-2's proof)

Mutation (`mapper/views/layered.py`, transient): the memo entry stores the SCALED
layout, `pos={nid: (card_w // 2 + int(cx * (card_w + gap)), lv) ...}`, so a hit
re-applies the scaling to already-scaled slots.

    $ python -B -m pytest -q -p no:cacheprovider "tests/test_perf_layout_memo.py::test_memo_invalidation_arms[title]" "tests/test_perf_layout_memo.py::test_memo_invalidation_arms[resize]"
    E           AssertionError: a widening title re-applies the scaling on the cached unscaled slots; caching the SCALED layout (M-R2c) reuses stale geometry and must fail this full-text compare
    tests\test_perf_layout_memo.py:252: AssertionError
    E       AssertionError: the resized render must byte-equal a fresh renderer's paint
    tests\test_perf_layout_memo.py:205: AssertionError
    FAILED tests/test_perf_layout_memo.py::test_memo_invalidation_arms[title] - A...
    FAILED tests/test_perf_layout_memo.py::test_memo_invalidation_arms[resize] - ...
    2 failed in 4.85s

`[title]` is now RED under M-R2c — the new renderer-level full-text compare sees the
stale scaled slots; the old region-clipped canvas compare could not (header-only
canvas, `r2-red.transcript` §5). `[resize]` stays RED as before.

RED -> restored (sha256 == 3e34fd90…e04743, §0) -> 2 passed GREEN (§1).

## 3 · RED proof — Y-ONLY clip (bus row not x-clipped)

Mutation (`mapper/canvas.py`, transient): `elbow_down`'s bus loop iterates
`range(xa + 1, xb)` — the pre-change unclipped form; the y spans stay clipped.

    $ python -B -m pytest -q -s -p no:cacheprovider tests/test_perf_paint_clip.py::test_wire_count_budget
    wire calls for l,j on wide-2000 at 118x34 (counter reset after mount): 23983998 (baseline 23983998, cap 61500)
    E       AssertionError: 23983998 wire calls for two keypresses exceeds the cap 61500 (baseline 23983998)
    1 failed in 17.45s

RED at the full unclipped baseline — the tightened cap still catches the y-only mutant
(the x-axis carries the whole gain). RED -> restored (sha256 == d354bd46…4838a2, §0).

