## 5 · RED proof — clip span WIDENED by a margin (partial-regression probe)

Mutation (`mapper/canvas.py`, transient): the vertical-drop clip bounds widened by a
16-cell margin each side, `range(max(0, y0 + 1 - 16), min(ybus + 16, self.h))` — the
clip keeps working but visits ~an extra span per edge. (A margin on the BUS row was
probed first and barely registers on this fixture — adjacent buses overlap — so the
drop span carries the probe; recorded plainly.)

    $ python -B -m pytest -q -s -p no:cacheprovider tests/test_perf_paint_clip.py::test_wire_count_budget
    wire calls for l,j on wide-2000 at 118x34 (counter reset after mount): 88226 (baseline 23983998, cap 61500)
    E       AssertionError: 88226 wire calls for two keypresses exceeds the cap 61500 (baseline 23983998)
    1 failed in 3.19s

RED: 88,226 ~= 7.2x the measured 12,264 — a partial clip regression, far below the
~24 M unclipped baseline, still fails the 5x-derived cap. (The old 1,200,000 cap would
have passed this mutant.) RED -> restored (sha256 == d354bd46…4838a2, §0) ->
`tests/test_perf_paint_clip.py` 17 passed GREEN.

## 6 · Note on the §1 arm of qa MED-2

The `[title]` arm's app-level canvas compare is KEPT (the emitted-form pin against the
fresh app session); the renderer-level compare is ADDED alongside it, so the arm now
bites at both levels. The `test_memo_invalidation_arms` docstring and the module
docstring say so.

